Allen Hung wrote:
> 
> A question about NFS:
>         NFS is developed base on UDP/IP protocols, and we all know NFS is Network
> file system. It means shared resources with others. But in my knowledge,
> UDP is unreliable,
> It means sometime the data on transferring maybe not correct?! So my
> question is:
> Why NFS was developed base on UDP, not TCP?

TCP is stream oriented, UDP is datagram oriented. TCP guarantees
delivery (or failure signal), UDP doesn't. Anybody using UDP has to make
his own checks. UDP is faster and more compact.

FTP is a stream oriented thing. File System (of any kind) isn't, I
guess.

Nix.





