Hello Paul

On Fri, 26 Jun 1998, you wrote:

> Can't remove the volume
> Error=ENO_MORE_MCELLS (-1055)
> Can't remove volume /dev/rz12e from domain 'usr_domain'

Some days ago I got similar messages althought not -1055 while removing
a volume. In my case there was no other way as to boot to SU and do
a /sbin/advfs/verify on that domain. This made possible to at least 
remove some but one volume.
Well, but if you are out of mcells you may try
to temporary add a (small) volume while adjusting the initial
Bitmap Metadata Table size and extend values. The man page for mkfdmn
and addvol are giving a hint for that. To not oversize these values
I took the average of blocks per file (see showfsets) and the size
of the volume to add (see disklabel). With the expected filelength for
that fileset/domain (hope your filesets in the domain are equally used)
calculate the expected number of files for that volume go to
the tables in man mkfdmn to get the recommended values for the "-p" and
"-x" arguments. Add this volume befor retrying to remove your rz12e.

To see, if the BMTs are growing/fragmenting do:
cd <mount-point-of-the-fileset>/.tags
/usr/sbin/showfiles -x M-<volindex*6>

For volindex please see showfdmn.
Although the grow size of the BMTs for each volume after DUNIX4.0 are
dynamically they seem not be be defragmented like the volume itself.


Best regards

