> to configure the mtools?
> How can I access the diskette drive?

A little spot of mess.

1. You can only mount devices with file systems recognized by the
running kernel.
   See your /sys/conf/<NAME> file for that.

   CDFS	= ISO 9660
   UFS	= Unix File System
   MFS	= AdvFS
   NFS	= Network File System

2. To mount a floppy, you have to build a file system on it first.
   Before that, you have to label it.

   disklabel -wr fd0 RX23
   newfs /dev/rfd0c

3. Then you can mount it

   mount -t ufs /dev/fd0c /floppy

4. In order to use MTools, you need to make the following:

   ln -s /dev/fd0c /dev/fddrive
   PATH=$PATH:/usr/bin/mtools

Nix.




