Billy Quinn wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
>         We are running Digital Unix 4.0b with the 6.1 CXX compiler and was
> wondering if anybody knows of a why to make the linker/loader tell you
> what symbols are unresolved ( and need to be extracted from other so's )
> . I used the ldd command to do this in Linux - but have not found a
> command as of yet on Digital Unix . Any ideas ? Thanks

At the shell prompt type:

	_RLD_ARGS=-trace <name-of-executable> <ENTER>

e.g.:

	$ _RLD_ARGS=-trace /bin/ls <ENTER>


For more info look at the man page loader(5).

Hope this helps,

