You need to create a directory called /etc/dt/config and copy
/usr/dt/config/{Xservers,Xconfig} into it. 

Then edit /etc/dt/config/Xservers and add the appropriate options to
the line that starts the X server.

Here's an example:

$ diff -c /etc/dt/config/Xservers /usr/dt/config/Xservers|more
*** Xservers    Fri Jun 12 11:11:24 1998
--- /usr/dt/config/Xservers     Tue Dec  9 05:27:26 1997
***************
*** 68,74 ****
  
  
  
!    :0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen 1280x1024 -vsync 60
  
  
  
--- 68,74 ----
  
  
  
!    :0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0


You will need to know what resolution and refresh your monitor is
capable of to set it up right.

-- 
Joel Gallun                             http://www.tux.org/~joel




