Cameron Laird wrote:
> 
> All of a sudden an enormous (14 megabyte) /etc/passwd.pag
> appeared in my file system.  What is this?  I moved it
> offline, and logins and related authentication all seem
> fine.  Anyone know what this is about?

Files:

/etc/passwd
/etc/passwd.dir
/etc/passwd.pag

The first is your "raw" password file. The other two are "hashed"
versions. Basically, if you have a lot of users, hashed password
database should speed up user lookup. If you use C2 security, the system
will try to use hashed version.

Still, I cannot understand how you got passwd.pag of 14 MB. What is the
size of passwd?

