SCSI-wise, there is no problem with Jaz drives. The problem is getting a
proper label on the disk. With 3.x, you can just create an entry in
/etc/disktab and use the disklabel command to label the cartridges.

With 4.x, this no longer works, so you have to write a proper disk label
another way. If you have some previously labeled cartridges, you can use
dd to copy the labels to new cartridges. Otherwise, you need a program
written by kevin.s.partin@boeing.com which writes a previously created
label to the disk.

e-mail me if you can't find a copy of this program.
