Kjell Andresen wrote:
> 
> Hello!
> 
> I've configured and initialized a set of raid5-disks on a
> raidcontroller, the KZPAC.
> 
> The device is visible in srm-mode and available if the machine is
> booted with genvmunix.
> 
> I build a new kernel in order to have a spesific kernel.
> 
> This kernel didn't support the re0, neither in the uerf-log nor by
> mounting raid#test / using "showfdmn -k fdmn"
> (/etc/fdmns/raid exists)
> 
> Does anybody known what to do e.g update /sys/conf/MACHINE,
> /etc/sysconfigtab or sysconfigdb?
> 

New devices still need to be linked into the kernel


The line I think you need is 
controller      xcr0    at *     vector xcrintr
                           ^^^ this is from genvmunix so it does not
name the card offset. The sizer command below will tell you.

Then optionally 
device disk             re0     at xcr0         drive 0
device disk             re1     at xcr0         drive 1
device disk             re2     at xcr0         drive 2
device disk             re3     at xcr0         drive 3
device disk             re4     at xcr0         drive 4
device disk             re5     at xcr0         drive 5
device disk             re6     at xcr0         drive 6
device disk             re7     at xcr0         drive 7
device disk             re8     at xcr1         drive 8

You could have gotten this info while booted with genvmunix
by running sizer -n t which will generate /tmp/t and /tmp/t.devs
edit /tmp/t and cut out the devices section from config vmunix
to the Pseudodevice section and replace the same section in your
current kernel config file /sys/conf/HOSTNAME rebuilt and boot
and you should be fine.

	Cheers
		Mark :)



