"Peter Tsang" <peter.hh.tsang@hkjc.org.hk> writes:


>We keep getting the following error message when
>we try to mount a NFS file set.

>>> Cannot MNT PRC: RPC: Program not registered

There is a typo in this error message, PRC should be RPC.  Still
pretty useless - it'll be improved somewhat in V5.0.

It means that the client tried to query mountd on the server, but
wasn't able to get the port number from the server's portmap.

>In this case, we try "rpcinfo -p nfs_server_name". We found
>a list of rpc process but without the 'nfs' (port # 100005).

"'nfs' (port # 100005)" is wrong.

  NFS is program 100003 and is always reegistered on port 2049.
MOUNT is program 100005 and is not on a particular port.

What you see is consistant with mountd not running on the server.

>Of course we have tried reboot the machines (both server and
>client) and it seems no use. 

>Any comments are appreciated.

On the server, what is in /etc/exports?  Is mountd running?  Are there
clues in /var/adm/syslog.dated/*/daemon.log?
