Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


The compiler has changed between V3.2G and V4.0D to DEC C. An
earlier version of this compiler was available in V3.2 by using
"cc -migrate". The old C compiler is still available in V4.0D as
"cc -oldc", although we recommend that you use the new compiler.

The default compilation mode in V4.0D is still -std0 (K&R), but
this is expected to also change in a future version. You may
override that using the comp.config file, if desired.

You can find more info on the new flags and features of DEC C
in the cc(1) man page and also in the online Programmer's Guide.

If you run into specific problems/questions, let us know.

-Jeff
