X-Deja-AN: 358934571
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
References: <ued8cxtc14.fsf@sobolev.dsm.fordham.edu>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


You will need to add -D_BSD to your CFLAGS, since the program
uses a version of wait3 that does not conform to the current
standard. (See the standards(5) man page for more information)
The standards refered to for these interfaces are:

  wait():  XPG4, XPG4-UNIX
  waitpid():  POSIX.1, XPG4-UNIX
  wait3():  XPG4-UNIX

The other interfaces are described in the wait3 man page. Look for
references to "backward compatible" in that man page and it will
describe the differences in <sys/resource.h>, etc.

I was able to build this on DIGITAL UNIX V4.0D by making this
change in the Makefile:

  CFLAGS  = $(DEBUG) $(CONFIG) -D_BSD

Let us know if you run into a problem with this solution.

-Jeff
