Andrei S. Koval wrote:
> 
> I have an Alpha Server with DU4.0A, and sometimes see messages
> in auth.log like:
> 
> ==============
> Jun  1 15:03:35 alpha syslog: gethostby*.getanswer: asked for "37.103.74.204.in-addr.arpa IN PTR",
> got type "CNAME"
> Jun  1 15:03:35 alpha syslog: gethostby*.getanswer: asked for "37.103.74.204.in-addr.arpa",
> got "37.32/27.103.74.204.in-addr.arpa"

These are reverse DNS queries. Your system is trying to determine the
hostname from the IP address it was given, when someone tried to telnet
to root account. This is normal for a decent UNIX system. And it
shouldn't report it, if everything was OK.

It looks like your DNS server is out of order, because the results of
those queries is incorect. Contact the person in charge of DNS service
in your network.

Nix.




