There have been some discussions of writing startup scripts recently, and
also about a year ago, on the alpha managers
list.

You should be aware that:
a) you need to know how to write code in the program your script is
starting which daemon'izes it correctly (closes its file descriptors,
change process group etc. etc.) Excellent code for doing this is given in
W. Stevens "Advanced Programming in the Unix
environment", Chapter 13. This book cannot be recommended too highly.
b) init sends the startup scripts HUP's; so your program will need to
ignore or handle SIGHUP, or it will go away immediately.

Hope this helps.

