Hi Asgar,

There is no easy way to do that.

I use 2 methods :

1) odump

$ odump -Dl /path_to_exe

This one gives the names of the .so, not the real path used by the
loader at exec time. But it works even if a .so is not found.

2) Traces on /sbin/loader
$ _RLD_ARGS=-v /path_to_exe <some option/arg that makes exe exits>

With this your LD_LIBRARY_PATH is taken into account. But the program is
started. You must know how to ask nothing to the program.
You could do : man loader to learn more options on /sbin/loader

Eric Dumazet
