Has anyone witnessed an excessive sys:usr CPU ratio. I am running
queries against a data warehouse on both UNIX 4.0d and 4.0b and getting
up to 98% sys cpu for the query processes. The database vendor can run
similar queries on a machine with no Advfs and obtain the usual 30:70
sys:usr ratio.

The database stats report very few logical IOs, suggesting the cache is
working correctly

I see this on all of our machines
        Alpha 1000 (128MB) Advfs, no RAID sets
        Alpha 4100 (1GB) 3 cpus, Advfs, HSZ controller for RAID-5 set
        Alpha 8400 (4GB) 10 cpus, Advfs, 3 HSZ controllers for RAID-5
sets

What could be the likely cause?
        
Many thanks

JP



