Asgar Ali wrote:
> 
> On DEC Unix V4, does anyone know the command that will display a list of
> libraries that an executable would use.
> ie command <exec name>   produces
> /usr/lib/xxx
> /usr/lib/xx
> /usr/directory/libalib.so  etc.

The /usr/bin/odump command will give you the libraries that are linked
against and executable, even other libraries:

% odump -D /usr/bin/X11/xterm | grep 'NEEDED:' | awk '{print $2}'
libXaw.so
libXmu.so
libXt.so
libSM.so
libICE.so
libXext.so
libX11.so
libc.so

also RPATH: will show you the alternate search path for the shared
libraries instead of the default.



