Hi,

Clustering is fairly complex, because it needs to handle some pretty
complex tasks. Even MS clustering is not trivial but the interface (the
clusteradmin) makes MS clusters a lot easier to configure and this is
only true if the application is cluster aware and has a cluster resource
DLL.
But back to the point, as stated in the other reply if you need the
system to be available you do not have much of a choice. I work for
Digital's Software Partner Engineering Group and my main focus is UNIX
clustering. I have developed a set of configurable PERL scripts for
certain partner applications. Unfortunately we currently do not have
this framework available for SAP, but it is for Oracle (both single
instance and parallel server). Digital's implementation of clustering is
most probably the best one around (and I don't say that because I work
for Digital, but I work for a Digital partner before where I had
exposure on a range of cluster solutions).

If you have any specific concerns I would be happy to address them, or
even if you just need more info feel free to EMAIL me, just remove the
NOSPAM from the mail address..

