You can try to fix this problem:

1. Create a directory with old (from DU3.x) libXt.so.
2. Write a wrapper script for each your application which
   reguires old libXt, like that

  # appl-wrapper-sript
  #!/bin/csh -f

  if ($?LD_LIBRARY_PATH) then
    setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH
/some/directory/with/old/libXt:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}
  else
    setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH /some/directory/with/old/libXt
  endif

  exec your.application

3. Launch your application through this script.


BTW, similar problem was with Netscape 3.1 some time ago.


