-r--r--r--   1 bin      bin        614400 Nov 17  1997 libXt.so
-r--r--r--   1 bin      bin         40960 Oct 10  1997 libnullplugin.so
-r-xr-xr-x   1 bin      bin         24576 Oct 10  1997 movemail*
drwxr-xr-x   2 bin      bin           512 Oct 10  1997 movemail-src/
-r-xr-xr-x   1 bin      bin          1304 Nov 17  1997 netscape*
-r-xr-xr-x   1 bin      bin       6250496 Oct 10  1997 real-netscape*

The shell script 'netscape' looks like:
% more /usr/local/bin/netscape-3.04/netscape
#!/bin/ksh

NAVDIR=`dirname $0`

uname -a | grep -q V4.0
if [ $? -eq 0 ]
then
    if [ -f $NAVDIR/libXt.so ]
    then
        export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$NAVDIR
    else
        echo "WARNING: This script can't find the modified X Toolkit library"
        echo "that is required for Java applets to function correctly."
        echo "You must either ensure that this script resides in the"
        echo "same directory as the modified libXt or modify this script"
        echo "to set the LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable to point to the"
        echo "alternate directory you've installed it in.  See the"
        echo "README.Digital file that came with this kit for more"
        echo "information."
        echo
        echo "Invoking Netscape, but don't expect Java to work..."
        echo
    fi

fi

if [ -x $NAVDIR/real-netscape ]
then
        exec $NAVDIR/real-netscape -name netscape  $*
else
        echo "ERROR: This script can't find the real-netscape binary."
        echo "You must either ensure that this script resides in the same"
        echo "directory as the real-netscape binary or modify this script"
        echo "to invoke the real-netscape binary from whatever alternate"
        echo "directory you've installed it in.  See the README.Digital"
        echo "file that came with this kit for more information."
        exit 0
fi

The real exectuable netscape is (re-)named 'real-netscape'.
I.e. netscape uses the "local" libXt.so library and the system library
(in /usr/lib) is not used.

