Did you remove the SUID root flag from xterm? This caused the same
strange spurious errors to me. It does not seem to be related to the
number of pty's in /dev; rather, xterm on DU seems to need root privileges 
on rare occasions (it will run without the SUID flag most of the time). 
Can anyone come up with an explanation for this? xterm under Linux, for
example, works perfect without any root privileges (and I use _lots_ of 
xterms simultaneously, frequently more then 64; I still wonder why they 
ship it SUID root).

