Subject: SUMMARY: DU v4's libXt is missing a few things
Date: 1998/06/05
Message-ID: <Eu2uzI.8oG@campus-news-reading.utoronto.ca>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 359815943
Sender: nntp@campus-news-reading.utoronto.ca (News)
X-Nntp-Posting-Host: rorqual.cita.utoronto.ca
References: <Eu18ur.JMz@campus-news-reading.utoronto.ca> <Eu1Gs2.Jt0@campus-news-reading.utoronto.ca>
Organization: Canadian Institute for Theoretical Astrophysics
Reply-To: mark@cita.utoronto.ca
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.windows.x


[  I sent this summary to the alpha-osf-managers mailing list yesterday, but
   just now realized that I'd forgotten to post it to comp.unix.osf.osf1 and
   comp.windows.x as well.  Besides the people named in the "thanks to" area
   below, various others have since forwarded similar replies.  Merci!  ]

Sigh.  Yet again, one of those things that seems so *obvious* once someone
holds it up in front of your face and shows it to you.  Next time I'll try
to *think* for a few more minutes before wasting everybody's time.  Anyway,
the solution is essentially ...

(1)  Copy the v3 libXt.so somewhere useful (I used /local/shlib).

(2)  Create a trivial wrapper script, which is nothing but

#!/bin/sh
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/local/shlib; export LD_LIBRARY_PATH
exec /our/real/application $*

Many thanks to ...

 Sean O'Connell <sean@stat.Duke.EDU>, whose reply was the first to arrive.

 Mike Iglesias <iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu>, who made essentially the same
 suggestion, and added that the problem may stem from the fact that DU v4
 is now X11R6-ish, whereas v3 was X11R5.

 Tom Blinn <tpb@zk3.dec.com>, who suspects that these old executables may
 date back to X11R3 days.

... as well as to all the rest of you, whose replies may be in transit but
haven't reached my mailbox yet.

(And many embarrassments, for not having come up with this solution myself!)

