> useless.
> 
> Can you give me your opinion about using AdvFS (+ LSM)?
> We do not have the polycenter PAK license.

I have had 2 years of experience with AdvFS. I like it a lot. Of course,
we have ADVFS-UTILITIES PAK, which enables enhanced features of AdvFS.

Without PAK your AdvFS will be somewhat crippled and I would strongly
advise you to get it.

As to physical failures of the disk... Well, if the whole disk crashes,
no File System will help you (except, of course, that AdvFS is easier to
backup than UFS, with the PAK).

I have recently had two disks create problems (bad sectors) under AdvFS.
The first disk was suspected earlier and the other had a "shower of
rain" a year ago (I'm amazed it lived so long). In both cases the whole
system crashed when it tried to access files on faulty blocks. 4.0D is
more friendly and I was able to locate the very file in question. I was,
however, able to boot both machines after the crash with the same disks.

To comment on your statement from above, if there is a physical problem
with the disk, then no file system can guarantee its consistence.

Nix.




